00:02:28.111 --> 00:02:29.420
So what does it mean?

00:02:29.421 --> 00:02:33.120
Cognitive appraisals
are a set of evaluations we

00:02:33.121 --> 00:02:36.550
go through in our mind, that
they can result in emotions.

00:02:36.551 --> 00:02:39.735
This is based on the appraisal
theory of emotions.

00:02:39.736 --> 00:02:42.650
For example,
if something happens and

00:02:42.651 --> 00:02:48.440
then we evaluate that
stimulus or event and first

00:02:48.441 --> 00:02:53.940
based on it's relevance, is it
relevant to me or my goals?

00:02:53.941 --> 00:02:55.390
If it's not relevant,
we don't care.

00:02:55.391 --> 00:02:57.350
So that doesn't
result in anything.

00:02:57.351 --> 00:03:00.318
But if it's relevant then we go
through further evaluations.

00:03:00.319 --> 00:03:05.230
For example, ok,
like for example,

00:03:05.231 --> 00:03:07.850
there's a change in
the stock market price.

00:03:07.851 --> 00:03:09.790
If you don't have any stocks,
you don't care.

00:03:09.791 --> 00:03:11.340
So that doesn't
result in anything.

00:03:11.341 --> 00:03:13.730
But then,
if you have then you check and

00:03:13.731 --> 00:03:16.860
you say, okay,
can I cope with this?

00:03:16.861 --> 00:03:19.250
Is it like did I
lose all my money or

00:03:19.251 --> 00:03:23.320
it was just a small drop and
then that's the coping

00:03:23.321 --> 00:03:25.010
potential, how
much you can cope.

00:03:25.011 --> 00:03:28.170
Is it something, for examples,
against your norms or

00:03:28.171 --> 00:03:31.400
values that also results
into something else?

00:03:31.401 --> 00:03:34.960
The way it works is through all
these evaluations in your mind,

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:38.670
you get to the point
of having emotions or

00:03:38.671 --> 00:03:41.140
having impure emotion changes.

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:47.910
So this psychologist Paul Sylvia
has pictures there, he

00:03:47.911 --> 00:03:51.600
studied the appraisal structure
of interest and he identified

00:03:51.601 --> 00:03:55.790
that novelty complexity and
coping potentials are the major

00:03:55.791 --> 00:04:00.040
appraisals that they result in
interest and what do they mean?

00:04:00.041 --> 00:04:03.224
Novelties, I guess it's more
clear if something is novel,

00:04:03.225 --> 00:04:05.390
it can be more interesting.

00:04:05.391 --> 00:04:07.980
The complexity,
is it the complex,

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:12.670
for example, he looked into
images and text, is it complex?

00:04:12.671 --> 00:04:14.680
Like poetry, is it complex?

00:04:14.681 --> 00:04:16.120
Is it comprehensible?

00:04:16.121 --> 00:04:20.413
The comprehensibility, he
identifies comprehensibility as

00:04:20.414 --> 00:04:23.820
the copy potential part for
this kind of stimuli.

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:28.650
So do we understand this has
